  "question": {
    "text": "In a region, the intensity of an electric field is given by $\\mathbf{E}=2 \\mathbf{i}+3 \\mathbf{j}+\\mathbf{k}$ in $\\mathrm{NC}^{-1}$. The electric flux through a surface $\\mathbf{S}=10 \\mathbf{i} \\mathrm{m}^{2}$ in the region is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$5 \\mathrm{Nm}^{2} \\mathrm{C}^{-1}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$10 \\mathrm{Nm}^{2} \\mathrm{C}^{-1}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$15 \\mathrm{Nm}^{2} \\mathrm{C}^{-1}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$20 \\mathrm{Nm}^{2} \\mathrm{C}^{-1}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $\\mathbf{E}=(2 \\mathbf{i}+3 \\mathbf{j}+\\mathbf{k}) \\mathrm{NC}^{-1}$\r\nand $\\quad \\mathrm{S}=10 \\mathrm{i} \\mathrm{m}^{2}$\r\nWe know that\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\\phi=\\mathbf{E} \\cdot \\mathbf{S} \\\\\r\n\\phi=(2 \\mathbf{i}+3 \\mathbf{j}+\\mathbf{k}) \\cdot(10 \\mathbf{i}) \\\\\r\n\\phi=20 \\mathrm{Nm}^{2} \\mathrm{C}^{-1}\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$"
  }
}